Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::controller_configuration_round_trips_the_page_size`.

The defect: `enabled_controller_configuration` shifts the Memory Page Size field to bit 8 instead
of bit 7. A 4 KiB page still encodes as 0 and passes, but every larger page lands one bit high, so
the controller reads twice the exponent the driver meant and walks each pointer in pages of the
wrong size.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(1u64 << (12 + ((configuration >> 7) & 0xf)), page_size_bytes)`.

diff --git a/src/configuration.rs b/src/configuration.rs
--- a/src/configuration.rs
+++ b/src/configuration.rs
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
         return None;
     }
     let memory_page_size = page_size_bytes.trailing_zeros() - 12;
-    Some(1 | memory_page_size << 7 | 6 << 16 | 4 << 20)
+    Some(1 | memory_page_size << 8 | 6 << 16 | 4 << 20)
 }
 
